  "scope": "One disposable kind v0.32.0 cluster using its bundled kindnet and Kubernetes v1.36.1; three case-owned namespaces with two non-root BusyBox clients and three inert HTTP Pods. The case proves the four model/training client-to-model-mirror/training-store TCP/8080 marker paths before policy; then applies pod-selected egress NetworkPolicies and proves model-client->model-mirror and training-client->training-store remain useful while the two cross-domain paths time out. A third listener serves separate /model and /training HTTP paths; a permitted model-client-to-listener network path can fetch both markers, demonstrating that native NetworkPolicy does not distinguish URI paths. No Services, DNS, external targets, IPv6, production CNI, external model/data sources, artifact integrity, TLS, application authorization, or production routing are evaluated. A denied probe is attributed only to this controlled scenario after healthy endpoints and a successful no-policy baseline; NetworkPolicy exposes no per-packet drop reason.",
